module gunbc.plans.realization_measurement_loop


fn realization_measurement_loop_body() -> List<std.markdown.MarkdownBlock> {
  [
    p(text: "**Status:** stable coordination plan · dispatch workers per phase · **DESIGN.md + the carriers remain the authority** — this doc is a worker-dispatch tracker, not a fact ledger, and each phase dissolves into a mark on its carrier when it lands (DESIGN §6 \"no parallel-ledger docs\"). A phase's real state is its branch/PR, not this file (mirrors `ROADMAP.md`)."),
    p(text: "**Owner:** unowned (original coordinator `zesty-deer-479` archived 2026-06-21) — operator-coordinated; consolidates the formerly-separate quick-ant-298 dependency-ordered roadmap (single authority, no fork). Linked from `ROADMAP.md` §2 *Minimal work — caching by realization*."),
    p(text: "**Companion plans** (same cost to schedule loop, different arm): the Schedule-width arm is detailed in [`resource-aware-scheduler.md`](resource-aware-scheduler.md) (larger allocations give larger throughput; `spawn_width = floor(available_memory / per_runnable_peak)`); the input-admission arm — the data side of the loop, gating which corpus a `WorkDemand` may accept — is detailed in [`input-envelope-roadmap.md`](input-envelope-roadmap.md) (`InputEnvelope = BoundedInput | EnvelopeUnknown`, fail-closed admission via `input_admitted`)."),
    hr(),
    h2(text: "0. Thesis — the substrate is shape-complete but input-starved"),
    p(text: "The realization layer is *fully modeled and almost entirely inert*: every carrier that should drive \"minimal work, as parallel as possible, guaranteed\" exists with the right type and is read by **no scheduler, fed by **no measurement, consulted by **no router. This is DESIGN §6's failure mode — *\"the tier where the machinery exists but nothing gates on it\"* — landed squarely on §1's **cost axis**."),
    p(text: "The fix is **one control loop**, not a pile of local patches (this is why §4 \"evaluate the whole pipeline\" is load-bearing, not a footnote):"),
    std.markdown.CodeBlock { code: "  measure (Phase 0)                    ← the keystone; makes cost a real fact\n    → CostAccount.time = Measured       (today: cost_account_predicted_zero())\n      → RealizationObjective Pareto over \{time, space, power, $\}\n         bounded by a deployment HardwareBudget (Phase 1 / Phase 3)\n        → Schedule width + shard balance + cache-layer choice\n          → total rolled up along the CRITICAL PATH, not the node sum (Phase 1.5)\n" },
    p(text: "The three notes from the operator are **not peers — they are a dependency chain rooted at measurement**: `minimal work` = §2 (cache planner) and `as parallel as possible` = §1 (width) can only be *optimized against a measured cost*, and `guaranteed` = §5 (measured, not predicted). Cost must become a measured fact before anything can plan against it. The independent CI audit reached the same conclusion (\"add the two-clock timing first\"); the dependency structure above is *why*."),
    h3(text: "The end-state acceptance gate (what the whole plan builds to)"),
    quote(blocks: [
      p(text: "For every pure transform `T` (resolve, parse, typecheck, *and* derived analyses like complexity-synthesis / affected-set — see `ROADMAP.md` §3 *Complexity / synthesis lens* and §4 *Testgen*), `realize(T)` returns a result content-addressed by `hash(inputs ⊕ content(T))`, materialized at the **minimal `Placement` spanning T's consumers (its reach)**. A transform that is **non-redundant** (shared across a layer boundary, or recompute-cost > cache-cost) with **no cache supplier at its reach layer** is a located, typed **ERROR** that emits a *request to provision a supplier there*. No silent `Recompute`; no under-keyed hit."),
    ]),
    p(text: "This is §5 (fail-closed) turned on the cost axis: uncached non-redundant work is not \"slow\", it is an *error*. The earliest truthful point to assert it is the **redundancy-only** cut (shared-across-boundary — needs reach, not measurement); the cost-based \"non-redundant\" half waits on measured cost (Phase 0 / §4). The phases below are the path to this gate; the dependency-ordered spine that maps work items onto it is in **§ Dependency-ordered spine** (before Sequencing)."),
    h3(text: "The invariant that governs every phase (DESIGN §3 / §4)"),
    quote(blocks: [
      p(text: "**Pure schedule TOPOLOGY stays central and deterministic; every measurement-fed decision is a PERIPHERAL realization.**"),
    ]),
    p(text: "The schedule (`Schedule = List<List<Runnable>>`) is a deterministic partial order — it expresses what *can* run in parallel, hardware-free, and is pinned by `std.realization_schedule` `schedule_eq` / `schedule_generates_identical_schedule`. A schedule whose *width or membership* depended on a measured per-machine `HardwareThreadCount` would break that equality across hosts. So: **measured ⇒ peripheral, by construction.** Width, shard balance, cache-layer choice, and the timing tap all live in the periphery (`extdeps/realization`, the host realizer), checked by *\"given these DeploymentFacts + these measured costs, the realizer picks X\"* witnesses — deterministic *given their inputs*. This is exactly what `std.realization_schedule` `CostAccount` anticipates. Most `.dag` programs are stateless/short-lived: they declare dependency structure and never mention hardware; the width-fold degenerates to \"just run it.\""),
    h3(text: "Realization has THREE dimensions (schedule · cache · compute-fabric)"),
    p(text: "\"Realization\" is one concept with three orthogonal-but-composed dimensions, **all keyed on the same content-addressed `ExecutionReceipt`**, all **peripheral** (§3), all governed by the **same measured cost + Pareto objective**:"),
    std.markdown.TableBlock {
      header: row(cells: [cell(text: "Dimension"), cell(text: "Carrier"), cell(text: "Asks"), cell(text: "§1 axis")]),
      alignments: [AlignNone, AlignNone, AlignNone, AlignNone],
      rows: [
        row(cells: [cell(text: "**schedule**"), cell(text: "`std.realization_schedule`"), cell(text: "*when / how parallel*"), cell(text: "parallel")]),
        row(cells: [cell(text: "**cache**"), cell(text: "`std.cache_interface`"), cell(text: "*whether it needs to run at all*"), cell(text: "§2 minimal work")]),
        row(cells: [cell(text: "**compute fabric**"), cell(text: "`product.compute_fabric`"), cell(text: "*where / on what it runs* (provision)"), cell(text: "placement / $")]),
      ],
    },
    p(text: "The proof they are dimensions of *one* concept rather than three separate models is **structural and already in the tree**: `std.cache_interface` `ExecutionReceiptRef` carries the cache-side reference, while `product.compute_fabric` `compute_fabric_resource_model_dissolution_receipt` records the retired heavy receipt surface and its content-hash successor obligation. The dimensions meet only at the receipt — never by direct coupling (§3/§4)."),
    p(text: "**The live compute-fabric interface is explicit demand → placement → supply.** `product.compute_fabric` `connect` takes a `ComputeNeed` and a `List<Opportunity>` and returns a `Connection`; there is no zero-argument inference/dispatch surface today. The desired no-user-wiring end state is future realization work: derive the need from the modeled execution and obtain opportunities from deployment facts before calling `connect`, parallel to cache-planner auto-wiring and the scheduler's hardware-budget fold. The plan must not describe that intended wiring as already landed."),
    p(text: "**Layering discipline (§3):** `compute_fabric` and `placement_supply` are **product**; schedule/cache are **std** (imports point toward std). Split: product owns host identity (`product.placement_supply.HostIdentity` only — `PlacementSupplyRow` converged/deleted, #6687) and std owns the `\{time,space,power\}` cost-axis measure carriers it composes; product `compute_fabric` owns the **$/billing axis** (`CostClass`, `MoneyMicros`) and projects fleet offers into that carrier; the **peripheral host realizer** bridges product→std and runs the Pareto pick. std stays product-free; hardware grants live in `std.machine_shape` + extdeps `shape_from_catalog`."),
    h3(text: "v2 is the target; v1 is the proving ground (DESIGN §7)"),
    p(text: "v1 (the Rust seed) is shrinking to zero; v2 (the self-hosted `.dag` compiler) is what must benefit. **Every phase's durable artifact is `.dag` that v2 inherits; the Rust seed is only the proving *handler* — where a host-effect attaches today, while v2 is mid-bootstrap and the v1 interpreter is still the only evaluator that actually runs.** You MAY edit v1 (it's a proving ground), but:"),
    quote(blocks: [
      p(text: "**The v2-benefit test:** if a phase's deliverable is a Rust patch with *no `.dag` model*, it failed. The carrier / lens / kernel / effect-shape is the artifact; the Rust code is one handler of it (§2 one-shape-N-handlers; §3 measured⇒peripheral; §7 Rust→zero)."),
    ]),
    p(text: "This is *why* the keystone's measurement is modeled as an **effect-shape + `PerformanceReceipt` carrier + a roll-up lens over the Node fold** (the same `fold_node` v2's own evaluator uses) — so when v2 self-hosts, the instrumentation, the cache kernel, the scheduler, and the fabric all come along for free. The Rust tap in `v1_interpreter.rs` *proves* the model green-by-execution today; it is the realization, not the authority. Per-phase split: **Phase 0** durable = the `.dag` measure model/lens, proving = the Rust eval tap; **Phase 1** durable = the `.dag` width-fold (`scheduler.dag` is already v2), proving = the `claim_executor` spawn cap; **Phase 1.5a/2/3** are already `.dag`-native (`v2.lens.affected_set`, the cache catalog/kernel, `compute_fabric`/`ci_yaml_emit`) — v2-inheriting by construction; only the cache *backends* (`resolved_graph_cache.rs`, `ParseTableMemo`) stay v1 handlers of the one `.dag` kernel."),
    hr(),
    h2(text: "Verified ground truth (module + symbol — do not re-derive)"),
    std.markdown.TableBlock {
      header: row(cells: [cell(text: "Fact"), cell(text: "Evidence")]),
      alignments: [AlignNone, AlignNone],
      rows: [
        row(cells: [cell(text: "Schedule width = full dependency frontier, **no capacity bound**"), cell(text: "`v2.std.dependency` `ReadinessLayer`; `v2.workflow.scheduler` `runnable_frontier_from_dependencies`")]),
        row(cells: [cell(text: "Thread-spawn **unbounded by hardware** (one OS thread per runnable-in-batch)"), cell(text: "`claim_executor.rs` `run_walk`")]),
        row(cells: [cell(text: "Corpus = **one** `RunnableDiscoveryBatch` node → serial `for` loop (293 witnesses invisible)"), cell(text: "`v2.workflow.ci_floor_plan` `corpus_runnable_for`; `cli_run.rs` `run_discovery_corpus_with_options_inner`")]),
        row(cells: [cell(text: "`CostAccount.total` is hardcoded zero"), cell(text: "`std.realization_schedule` `cost_account_predicted_zero`; `CostBasis` / `Measured`")]),
        row(cells: [cell(text: "Single eval seam exists; per-variant self-time tap already there, **not** content-hash-keyed, **not** fed to CostAccount"), cell(text: "`v1_interpreter.rs` `eval_expr`; `eval_profile_snapshot` (keys by `expr_variant_index`)")]),
        row(cells: [cell(text: "Floor timing persists per-entry resolve + per-witness evaluation receipts, rolls up both totals, and renders timing histograms"), cell(text: "`cli_run.rs` `DiscoverySummary`, `project_witness_cost_receipt`; `claim_executor.rs` `run_discovery_batch_node`, `render_timing_histogram`")]),
        row(cells: [cell(text: "Cache catalog has **zero runtime consumers**; `CacheLayerPlan` unused"), cell(text: "`std.cache_interface` `CacheLayerPlan`; `plan_cache_layers`")]),
        row(cells: [cell(text: "3 live caches hand-wired, **3 different key derivations**"), cell(text: "`resolved_graph_cache.rs` `derive_subject_digest` (content-hash); `v1_interpreter.rs` `ParseTableMemo` (in-proc map); `pure_call_memo_key` keys by **address** `(usize,Vec<usize>)` not hash; sccache external")]),
        row(cells: [cell(text: "Carrier for hardware budget **already exists**"), cell(text: "`std.measure` `HardwareThreadCount`; `extdeps.cpu.machine_shape` `shape_from_catalog`; `extdeps.cpu.types` `CpuDeploymentFacts`")]),
        row(cells: [cell(text: "Pareto kernel + objective vocabulary already shared"), cell(text: "`std.pareto` `dominance_of_comparisons`, `AxisGoal`; `std.realization_schedule` `RealizationObjective`")]),
        row(cells: [cell(text: "Runner model exists; ci.yml **is generated + byte-drift-gated**"), cell(text: "`extdeps.github.actions` `RunnerSpec`; generator = `gunbc.ci_yaml_emit` `expected_ci_yml`, parse-validate = `gunbc.ci_yaml_validate` `ci_yml_parses`, and `gunbc.generated_artifact` `committed_generated_artifacts` enrolls generated artifacts in drift checking. `extdeps.github.ci` `github_actions_workflows_dir` supersedes the former stale \"hand-edited\" comment. `runs-on: [self-hosted,linux,arm64]` is emitted as a **literal** today — the seam Phase 3a routes through `RunnerSpec`")]),
        row(cells: [cell(text: "A 3rd (richest) measured-time carrier already exists"), cell(text: "`gunbc.fleet_intent` `PerformanceReceipt`, `MeasurementConfidence`; `gunbc.ci_fleet` `ComputeSupplyFacts.observed_performance`")]),
        row(cells: [cell(text: "`ExecutionReceipt` digest is **itself a stub** (not yet a content hash)"), cell(text: "`product.compute_fabric` `compute_fabric_resource_model_dissolution_receipt` records the retired `execution_receipt_digest` stub")]),
        row(cells: [cell(text: "Compute demand has a live model home; corpus sharding is not represented yet"), cell(text: "`product.compute_fabric` `Program`, `HardRequirements`, `ComputeNeed`")]),
        row(cells: [cell(text: "srv1/srv2 public offers are modeled in gunbc; credentials and secret per-host configuration remain ctrl-tier"), cell(text: "`gunbc.ci_fleet` `srv1_offer`, `srv2_offer`; ctrl `plans.fabric.operator_fleet`")]),
        row(cells: [cell(text: "compute fabric = need→opportunity connection market; provisioning is `connect(need, opportunities)` and returns a `Connection`"), cell(text: "`product.compute_fabric` `ComputeNeed`, `Opportunity`, `Connection`, `connect`")]),
        row(cells: [cell(text: "Map→reduce execution decomposition remains open; the live program model stops at identity + hard requirements"), cell(text: "`product.compute_fabric` `Program`, `HardRequirements`")]),
      ],
    },
    hr(),
    h2(text: "Phase 0 — Measured cost (THE KEYSTONE)"),
    p(text: "**Goal:** flip `CostAccount.time` from `predicted_zero` to `Measured`. Everything quantitative depends on this. NB: the timing *primitives already exist* — this is **\"wire the existing tap to a content-hash key + CostAccount,\"** not \"build timing from scratch.\""),
    ul(items: [
      li(text: "**Grain decision (settled this session): key on the content-hash of the cache SUBJECT, not per-AST-node, not per-variant.** Rationale: the `Node` is an `Rc<Node>` with **no ambient content-hash** (today the profiler keys by `expr_variant_index`), so per-node hashing at `eval_expr` is *not free* and would perturb the measurement (§5 observer effect). The cache-subject frame is exactly where a content-hash *is already computed*, and it is the grain the scheduler (per-Runnable) and the cache router (per-subject recompute cost) both consume — so per-subject is the §2 \"model once, derive every use\" point: per-Runnable is its aggregate, per-variant its `group-by`, full per-node an **opt-in deep projection** over the same seam. Per-variant counters are a *dead end* (a variant is not a cacheable identity → can't feed Phase 2)."),
      li(text: "**Instrumentation = the dual of the cache.** Both wrap the same fold boundary keyed by the same content-hash: the cache stores node→value, the instrument stores node→duration. The *analysis* is a pure lens; the measurement itself is a §1 host-effect. Use `v1_interpreter.rs` `eval_expr` / `eval_profile_snapshot` for the existing gross−children self-time decomposition."),
      li(text: "**The measurement output is a `PerformanceReceipt`, NOT a new struct (§3 — do not coin a 4th).** The observation carrier already exists at `gunbc.fleet_intent` `PerformanceReceipt` with `MeasurementConfidence`. So Phase 0 emits a `PerformanceReceipt` keyed by the cache-subject hash → it rolls up into `CostAccount.time` (the aggregate). This is what *fuses the keystone to the compute-fabric deliverable*: the thing Phase 0 measures **is** the fabric's execution receipt, and `MeasurementConfidence` (SingleSample/Range/DistributionSummary) is exactly the per-witness-distribution honesty the audit's observability gap needs."),
      li(text: "**Feed `CostAccount`.** `std.realization_schedule` `CostBasis` already distinguishes `Measured` / `Predicted`; aggregate PerformanceReceipts → `RealizationPlan.total`."),
      li(text: "**Converge the time authorities — there are THREE, not two (§3).** `std.verification` `NanosecondDuration` is the authority. The former millisecond `measured_ms` field has **dissolved** into the nanosecond budget predicate carried by `std.verification` `TestNodeCostDimension.measured_time`, not a parallel measured field (ms truncates a 5 ns step to 0 — DESIGN §6). And `gunbc.fleet_intent` `PerformanceReceipt.cost` is the *observation* feeding the roll-up — observation vs roll-up, not a fork. Net: one observation carrier (`PerformanceReceipt`), one roll-up (`CostAccount.time`), `measured_ms` deleted."),
      li(text: "**Timing persistence LANDED.** `cli_run.rs` `DiscoverySummary` carries per-entry resolve receipts, per-witness `PerformanceReceipt`s, and both totals; `claim_executor.rs` `run_discovery_batch_node` consumes them and `render_timing_histogram` renders the two-clock view. The remaining Phase 0 work is the content-hash identity + modeled `CostAccount` integration, not receipt transport."),
      li(text: "**§5 gate:** purity oracle — witness verdicts byte-identical instrumented vs not."),
      li(text: "**Dissolution trigger:** `cost_account_predicted_zero()` has no callers on the floor path; `measured_ms` deleted."),
    ]),
    hr(),
    h2(text: "Phase 1 — Make parallelism visible + hardware-bounded width  (note 1)"),
    p(text: "**Depends on:** Phase 0 (shard balance needs measured per-shard cost)."),
    ul(items: [
      li(text: "**Explode the corpus node** (`v2.workflow.ci_floor_plan` `corpus_runnable_for`) into per-entry-group `Runnable`s — **rows, not Rust**. The retired demand surface is recorded by `product.compute_fabric` `compute_fabric_resource_model_dissolution_receipt`; reuse its grounded successor rather than minting a scheduler-local shard list. Shard *by whole entry-group* to preserve the warm `typed_module_cache` (splitting an entry's witnesses re-incurs its cold resolve). This is the keystone both background audits independently named."),
      li(text: "**The hardware budget is what `compute_fabric` PROVISIONS — do not coin a fresh carrier (§2/§3).** The width-fold reads `extdeps.cpu.machine_shape` `shape_from_catalog`. **The width decision *is* a placement decision:** `product.compute_fabric` `connect` places a `ComputeNeed` on an `Opportunity`. So this phase is co-designed with Phase 3 (compute_fabric is the provisioning interface; the runner *declares* the offer, the scheduler *consumes* the placement — one market, two readers). DFS `std.machine_shape` + `extdeps.cpu.types` `CpuDeploymentFacts` before extending; do **not** invent `DeploymentFacts`."),
      li(text: "**The width-fold.** Schedule stays the pure partial order; a peripheral realizer folds it against the `HardwareBudget` → actual width, a Pareto pick over `\{wall-time↓, peak-memory↓\}` bounded by `width ≤ cores` — reusing `std.pareto` + `RealizationObjective.goals` (already `List<AxisGoal>` — wiring carriers that already speak the same vocabulary, not inventing one)."),
      li(text: "**Bound the spawner** (`claim_executor.rs` `run_walk`) by `available_parallelism`/budget — fixes the *dual* hazard: under-parallel (serial corpus) **and** over-parallel (unbounded spawn on a wide batch)."),
      li(text: "**Determinism:** schedule topology stays witness-stable; width/shard are peripheral, checked by given-these-facts witnesses."),
      li(text: "**Dissolution trigger:** the corpus is ≥2 runnables in the schedule; the spawner reads a budget."),
    ]),
    hr(),
    h2(text: "Phase 1.5 — Holistic cleanups (note 4)  ·  mostly parallel to 1"),
    ul(items: [
      li(text: "**Wire `affected_set` into the corpus + gate roster** (audit lever #1). The compile-time, fail-closed `v2.lens.affected_set` + runner + superset proof exist and are green but unimported. Skip only on a content-addressed match to a verified-green baseline; **fail closed** on any miss. Biggest wall-clock lever on PR branches. (Independent of Phase 0.)"),
      li(text: "**`total` = measured critical-path roll-up** (note 4): weights a short phase *on the critical path* (the perturb gate) at full cost and a short phase *hidden under a parallel branch* at ~0. (Needs Phase 0.)"),
      li(text: "**Collapse the perturb cold-recompile** (~14 s, fail-fast root, critical path): resolve the planted (fresh-name, unimported) module against the green compile's index instead of `cp -r dag` + cold rebuild; preserves the discriminating-red (§5). (Independent of Phase 0.)"),
    ]),
    hr(),
    h2(text: "Phase 2 — Cache-layer planner: the catalog's first consumer  (note 2)"),
    p(text: "**Depends on:** Phase 0 (cost-aware reach needs measured recompute cost)."),
    ul(items: [
      li(text: "**Land the planner the catalog promises** (`std.cache_interface` `plan_cache_layers`). Given the `CacheInterfaceFacts` rows + a deployment's *available* backends, emit a `CacheLayerPlan`: L1 in-process → L2 sccache / cargo target / resolved-graph → L3 CAS."),
      li(text: "**One content-address lookup kernel, N backends bound by `transport_encoding`** (§4 one-kernel/N-handlers). The in-process memo is just the `InProcess` row of the *same* kernel. **Converge the key derivations onto ONE content-addressed subject identity.** Today there are *four* keyings: `parse_cache` by path, `typed_module_cache` by module-name, `resolved_graph` by content-hash, `pure_call_memo` by address — **and the retired `ExecutionReceipt` digest the whole three-dimension unification rested on was itself a 4th stub**, recorded by `product.compute_fabric` `compute_fabric_resource_model_dissolution_receipt`. The §0 thesis (\"all three dimensions keyed on one `ExecutionReceipt`\") is only *true once this digest becomes a real content hash aligned with the cache-subject identity* — so this convergence is shared work between Phase 2 (cache) and the compute-fabric track, not cache-local. The `key_derivation` axis exists for exactly this."),
      li(text: "**Cost-aware reach (§1).** Reach for a layer only when its predicted delta favors it: `min(recompute, lookup + p(miss)·recompute)` — `read_latency` (InProcessNs…WanTensMs) is already a modeled axis; `recompute` comes from Phase 0. A WAN CAS hit can lose to recomputing a cheap node."),
      li(text: "**Auto-wire (the operator's \"user shouldn't wire it themselves\").** The deployment declares which backends it offers; the planner emits the wiring — dissolving the bespoke `if sccache --show-stats` shell in `ci.yml` and the `GUNBC_RESOLVED_GRAPH_CACHE_DIR` env read."),
      li(text: "**Fail-closed (§5).** A backend probe that is absent/unauthorized falls through to the next layer → ultimately recompute, **never** serves a stale/unverified hit (`CacheRejectReason` already enumerates `BackendUnavailable`/`BackendUnauthorized`). Verdict-identity, not byte-identity, until the deferred canonical-byte compare lands — so do NOT route emit/lower consumers through it yet."),
      li(text: "**First free measurement:** un-dormant `resolved_graph_cache` in CI (read by the seed, unset in `ci.yml`) as a warm A/B."),
      li(text: "**Dissolution trigger:** `ci.yml` carries no hand-wired cache shell; one lookup kernel; one subject key."),
    ]),
    hr(),
    h2(text: "Phase 3 — Infra / deployment onto `.dag` (srv1 / srv2)  ·  the second ask"),
    p(text: "**Goal:** model the actual infra/deployment — runner config, access, host config — as **data**, dissolving bespoke `ci.yml` shell + manual runner setup. **\"Get CI onto `.dag`\" = instantiate the fabric for srv1/srv2:** `gunbc.ci_fleet` `ComputeOffer` models self-hosted offers; `gunbc.fleet_intent` `ContainerRuntime` enumerates cloud realizations. This meets note 1 at the placement carrier — the offer the runner *declares* is the budget Phase 1's scheduler *consumes*."),
    p(text: "**§3 boundary — THREE tiers, not two (refined after the #5177 review).** The operator's rule: keep the *generic* \"CI runner\" cleanly apart from *our* CI runner; CI does not need to know our fleet. So:"),
    ul(items: [
      li(text: "**3a-generic — \"CI runner\" in the abstract (any project).** What we expect *any* CI runner to do, project-agnostic: **a workflow triggered by an event** (`trigger → workflow`), realized per platform. The GHA realization already exists — `extdeps.github.actions` `Workflow`, `WorkflowTrigger`, and `RunnerSpec`. The **generic `offer → RunnerSpec` projection** (`gunbc.runner_spec_from_offer` `runner_spec_from_offer`, kernel/arch → labels) belongs HERE, next to `RunnerSpec` in the generalized layer — it works for *any* fleet offer. **This tier MUST NOT import a concrete SKU (`extdeps.cpu.ampere`) or name srv1/srv2.** (GitLab/Buildkite/etc. would be sibling platform handlers — one generic interface, N realizations, §2/§4.)"),
      li(text: "**3a-ours — OUR gunbc CI runner (our repo's META-modeling).** OUR workflow instance + OUR fleet: the srv1/srv2 *instantiation* (the Ampere-Altra `ComputeOffer`, the `gunbc-ci-fleet` identity, the per-thread Hz). This **must live in a file that is gunbc's own meta-model** (`dag/gunbc/ci_*`), and it *consumes* the 3a-generic interface — it is where the concrete SKU import is legitimate. The srv1/srv2 instantiation meta-model is public-in-our-repo; only secrets cross into ctrl."),
      li(text: "**3b — ctrl concrete fleet (private).** Access creds, runner registration tokens, and truly-secret per-host config live in **ctrl `plans.fabric.operator_fleet`**; public host offers remain `gunbc.ci_fleet` `srv1_offer` / `srv2_offer`. Secret rows instantiate the 3a-ours meta-model."),
    ]),
    p(text: "**#5177's separation is complete.** The live generic projection is `gunbc.runner_spec_from_offer` `runner_spec_from_offer`: it derives a `RunnerSpec` from any `ComputeOffer` without importing a concrete SKU or naming srv1/srv2. Gunbc's concrete fleet remains in `gunbc.ci_fleet` `gunbc_ci_fleet_offer`, and `gunbc.ci_runner_target` `gunbc_ci_selected_runner_spec` projects the selected target through that generic seam. `gunbc.ci_workflow` consumes the selected runner spec; `gunbc.ci_yaml_emit` `expected_ci_yml` and `gunbc.ci_yaml_validate` `ci_yml_parses` keep ci.yml generated and checked. Future work extends those live symbols rather than any retired module path."),
    p(text: "**Dissolution trigger:** `.github/workflows/ci.yml` is emitted from a `.dag` spec whose runner block is *our* fleet offer projected through the *generic* `offer → RunnerSpec` seam (no hand-authored runner block, no fleet SKU in the generic tier); the `HardwareBudget` the scheduler reads is the one *our* offer declares."),
    hr(),
    h2(text: "Dependency-ordered spine (foundation → end state)"),
    p(text: "The work-item view of the phases above, ordered by dependency toward the acceptance gate (absorbed from the former quick-ant-298 roadmap; maps onto the phases, does not replace them)."),
    ul(items: [
      li(text: "**F1** scheduler gives heavy nodes the budgeted width — *#5421 merged* (= Phase 1 width landing)."),
      li(text: "**F2/F3** key-completeness lens (`ToolchainChange ∈ triggers ⟹ input ∈ inputs_considered`) + `resolved_graph` keyed by construction — *#5423, in review* (= the Phase 2 key-derivation axis, spec-level)."),
      li(text: "**P1 — honest keys, verified by execution** *(deps F2,F3)*: realizer-key lens (executed digest ⊇ declared `inputs_considered`, RED otherwise — would have caught the `from_utf8_lossy` collision); stable transform-id (reproducible source/commit/tree hash, not binary bytes); census parity for `parse_table_memo`. (= Phase 2 \"converge key derivations\".)"),
      li(text: "**P2 — one door: caching by inhabitance** *(deps P1)*: `realize(subject)` as the sole API; eliminate raw bypass (`build_multi_entry_index`, hand-rolled `ParseTable` HashMap → inhabited via `realize`, DESIGN §6's own example). (= Phase 2 one-kernel/N-backends.)"),
      li(text: "**P3 — reach → layer + completeness fail-closed** *(deps P2)* — **the core ask / the acceptance gate**: reach analysis lens (consumer set + boundary → minimal sufficient `Placement`); completeness gate (subject realized below reach → ERROR; non-redundant transform with no supplier at reach → ERROR — **land the redundancy-only cut first**, cost half waits on §4); supplier provisioning + typed request."),
      li(text: "**P4 — economic tier** *(deps Phase 0 measurement)*: per-transform measured cost (`PerformanceReceipt` → cost-aware reach); `Materialization` = `Recompute | Memoize | Share` chosen by measured cost."),
      li(text: "**P5 — v2 dissolution** *(deps B2)*: `content(T) = content_hash(subgraph)` native; dissolves the binary-hash/version-string approximations and makes P1's spec↔realizer check structural."),
    ]),
    p(text: "**External blockers (track as work-items):** **B1** #5295 generic-instantiation (FreeMonoid<T> cached without variants — itself an under-keyed in-proc cache) → gates cross-shard `Share` (Phase 2.2). **B2** v2 cross-tree content-hash (\"increment 4\", the `ContentHash` subject on `RealizedStep`; cf. `product.compute_fabric` `compute_fabric_resource_model_dissolution_receipt` for the retired `execution_receipt_digest` stub) → gates P5."),
    p(text: "**Critical path:** `F2/F3 → P1 → P2 → P3 (redundancy cut) → P3 supplier`. `P1.census`, `P4`, and Phase-2 sub-items parallelize off it; cross-shard `Share` and P5 wait on B1/B2. The redundancy-only P3 cut is the earliest point \"uncached non-redundant work is an error\" is truthful — it needs reach, not the cost model."),
    h2(text: "Sequencing & dispatch"),
    std.markdown.CodeBlock { code: "        ┌─────────────── Phase 0 (keystone: measured cost) ───────────────┐\n        │                                                                  │\n   Phase 1.5a (affected_set)   Phase 1 (visible parallelism      Phase 2 (cache planner)\n   Phase 1.5c (perturb)        + hardware-bounded width)          │\n   — independent of 0          │                                  │\n        │                  Phase 1.5b (critical-path total) ←──────┘ (needs 0)\n        │\n   Phase 3a (runner schema + ci.yml gen)  — HardwareBudget carrier co-designed with Phase 1\n        │\n   Phase 3b (ctrl: srv1/srv2 concrete) — private, separate repo\n" },
    std.markdown.TableBlock {
      header: row(cells: [cell(text: "Phase"), cell(text: "Depends on"), cell(text: "Intricacy / Volume"), cell(text: "Notes")]),
      alignments: [AlignNone, AlignNone, AlignNone, AlignNone],
      rows: [
        row(cells: [cell(text: "0 keystone"), cell(text: "—"), cell(text: "high / medium"), cell(text: "root of everything quantitative; load-bearing seam (`v1_interpreter.rs`, escalate per DESIGN)")]),
        row(cells: [cell(text: "1 visible parallelism + width"), cell(text: "0"), cell(text: "high / medium"), cell(text: "shares `HardwareBudget` carrier with 3a")]),
        row(cells: [cell(text: "1.5a affected_set"), cell(text: "—"), cell(text: "medium / small"), cell(text: "fail-closed; can start now")]),
        row(cells: [cell(text: "1.5b critical-path total"), cell(text: "0"), cell(text: "medium / small"), cell(text: "")]),
        row(cells: [cell(text: "1.5c perturb collapse"), cell(text: "—"), cell(text: "medium / small"), cell(text: "can start now")]),
        row(cells: [cell(text: "2 cache planner"), cell(text: "0"), cell(text: "high / large"), cell(text: "converges 3 key derivations; first catalog consumer")]),
        row(cells: [cell(text: "3a runner schema + ci.yml gen"), cell(text: "(1 for budget carrier)"), cell(text: "high / large"), cell(text: "public; extends `CiFloorSpec` emission")]),
        row(cells: [cell(text: "3b ctrl srv1/srv2"), cell(text: "3a"), cell(text: "—"), cell(text: "**private `~/ctrl`**, separate PR")]),
      ],
    },
    p(text: "**Start-now lanes (no measurement dependency):** 1.5a (affected_set), 1.5c (perturb), and 3a schema groundwork. **Critical path:** Phase 0 → 1 / 2."),
    hr(),
    h2(text: "Guardrails for every worker (DESIGN)"),
    ul(items: [
      li(text: "**Pure central spec, peripheral measured realization** (the §3 invariant above). Anything measured is peripheral — never in the schedule topology the `schedule_eq` witnesses pin."),
      li(text: "**DFS existing carriers before minting** (§2/§3): `std.machine_shape`, `CpuDeploymentFacts`, `RunnerSpec`, the cache catalog, `std.pareto`, `RealizationObjective.goals`. The vocabulary mostly exists — wire it, don't re-coin it. (Background verification specifically flagged: do not invent a fresh `DeploymentFacts`.)"),
      li(text: "**Rows, not Rust** — express new schedule/cache/runner facts as data; do not cement the seed to satisfy a ratchet (the ratchet is downstream of substrate migration)."),
      li(text: "**v2-benefit test (§7)** — the durable artifact is `.dag` that v2 inherits; the Rust seed is only the proving *handler*. A deliverable that is a Rust patch with no `.dag` model failed. (See the §0 \"v2 is the target\" principle.)"),
      li(text: "**Fail-closed (§5)** + **purity oracle** on every memo/measurement (byte-identical warm-vs-cold; verdict identical instrumented-vs-not). A bounded \"forever\" ≠ an \"unknown\" error."),
      li(text: "**Green by execution, not spec-without-execution.** A real consumer runs green + a discriminating input goes red. Typecheck + grep are not consumers."),
      li(text: "**Each phase lands with a named dissolution trigger; the mark is on the carrier.** This doc is coordination only; delete its entry when the carrier records the fact."),
      li(text: "**Load-bearing files** (DESIGN-named pipeline stages, substrate types, gates: `v1_interpreter.rs`, `cli_run.rs`, the scheduler, `realization_schedule.dag`) carry a higher bar — escalate before touching under a brief that pre-dates the relevant model PR."),
    ]),
    h2(text: "Open decisions to confirm before scoping the affected phase"),
    ol(items: [
      li(text: "**Placement/budget carrier** — extend `compute_fabric`'s `satisfies` + `std.machine_shape` grant with the thread-count/Pareto dimension (the width decision = a placement decision), vs a sibling carrier? (DFS task in Phase 1 / 3a.) Do not invent `DeploymentFacts`."),
      li(text: "**The $/billing cost axis crosses the std↔product line.** std `CostAccount` carries `\{time,space,power\}`; the $ axis (`CostClass`, `MoneyMicros`) lives in product `compute_fabric`. Confirm: the std schedule's objective stays `\{time,space,power\}`; the **peripheral host realizer** combines it with the product $ axis for the full Pareto pick. (Keeps std product-free.)"),
      li(text: "**Cache planner timing** — the *plan* (which layers, what order) can be compile-time data; only the *availability probe* is runtime/peripheral. Confirm the split when scoping Phase 2."),
      li(text: "**Runner-label vocabulary** — how far to close `SelfHosted\{labels: List<String>\}` toward a typed topology / a `compute_fabric` offer (3a) without over-fitting to srv1/srv2 (which live in ctrl)."),
      li(text: "**Sharding belongs in the demand model — Phase 1 and 3 must meet there, not just at the budget.** The live `product.compute_fabric` `Program` / `ComputeNeed` authority models identity and hard requirements but not sharding yet; extend that authority for the corpus `RunnableDiscoveryBatch` rather than minting a scheduler-local shard list."),
    ]),
  ]
}

data realization_measurement_loop_plan: gunbc.plan.Plan = gunbc.plan.Plan {
  slug: "realization-measurement-loop",
  title: "Plan — Realization & Measurement: closing the cost → schedule loop (+ infra onto `.dag`)",
  body: realization_measurement_loop_body(),
  retirement: gunbc.plan.PlanRetiresWhen { condition: unbound_dissolution(description: "Delete this plan once the cost→schedule loop is closed — every pure transform's realize(T) is content-addressed by hash(inputs ⊕ content(T)) and materialized at its minimal Placement, CostAccount is fed by Measured basis (not hardcoded zero), schedule width is hardware-bounded and the spawner is bounded by available_parallelism, the cache catalog has live runtime consumers, and a non-redundant transform with no cache supplier at its reach is a located typed ERROR — so the substrate is measurement-fed rather than input-starved.")
  }
}
